cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Band-Gap Observatory"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the repository and the archived release."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Putradi"
    given-names: "James Nikolas"
    alias: "JoeyHammoth"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoeyHammoth/semiconductor-bandgap-belvedere"
url: "https://joeyhammoth.github.io/semiconductor-bandgap-belvedere/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A browser-native, zero-backend inference and experiment-design instrument for
  undergraduate diode thermometry: sloppy-model analysis, microcanonical HMC,
  nested sampling, Stein variational inference, optimal transport, state-space
  models and amortised neural posteriors, with a GPU-rendered interface.
keywords:
  - band gap
  - diode thermometry
  - Bayesian inference
  - nested sampling
  - sloppy models
  - WebAssembly
  - WebGPU
version: 0.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
